From 0036f23fcd2bbc0e38e702e20ec230f01adeb4ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:06:29 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] kcm_kwin_scripts: script list filled after the page is
 shown (deferred scan, busy indicator after 150 ms)

Page type: List (docs/page-design.md). kwinrc keys ([Plugins] <name>Enabled, [Script-<name>]), KPackage
install/uninstall, D-Bus /Scripting start and the config dialog are unchanged.

Moved / renamed:
- "Get New..." is now "Get New Scripts..." (kcm_kwin_scripts/get-new). Install from File... kept.
- Search field got a Kirigami.ContextualHelpButton beside it (new short text: what scripts are, Configure..., deletes
  apply on Apply). Status InlineMessage stays first. Icon-only/Install actions got Accessible.name.
- Empty list: PluginSelector already shows its own "No plugins found" placeholder.
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_kwin_scripts.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 8 rows ok, 0 lost.

Speed (cause from code, not measured):
- Module::load() called KWinScriptsData::pluginMetaDataList() (KPackage findPackages("KWin/Script") reads the metadata
  of every installed script) and KPluginModel::addPlugins() (findConfig() per script, a QPluginLoader probe;
  kcmutils/src/core/kpluginmodel.cpp:190-204), both synchronously before the first frame.
- Now load() only clears state; the scan and addPlugins run one event-loop turn later (QTimer::singleShot(0)), with a
  generation counter so a newer load/import/GHNS refresh cancels a pending fill. New property kcm.loading drives a
  BusyIndicator shown only after 150 ms. Not moved to a worker thread: KPackage::PackageLoader thread safety could not
  be checked here (no kpackage source in the tree), so I kept it on the GUI thread.
- Not changed: KWinScriptsData::isDefaults() still rescans packages (used by the shell's changed-settings marker).
- Numbers: before (build/bench/clean/before-slow.tsv, under load) 702 ms first frame at 0.5 CPU. After: pending,
  manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-019, HIG-020, HIG-047, HIG-058.

Not built yet (freeze).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
